        "title": "Body found in Derry bog decapitated more than 2,000 years ago, coroner finds",
        "source": "The Guardian - Science",
        "source_id": "guardian_science",
        "category": "culture",
        "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/nov/18/ballymacombs-more-woman-derry-bog-decapitated-2000-years-ago",
        "published_at": "2026-11-18T08:00:36",
        "level": "C2",
        "slot_level": "C2",
        "source_level": "C2",
        "word_count": 510,
        "duration_sec": null,
        "body_text": "A coroner’s investigation into Northern Ireland’s most venerable cold case has concluded that the victim was decapitated more than 2,000 years ago. The inquest-style inquiry determined that Ballymacombs More Woman – the name given to iron age remains found in a County Derry bog three years ago – was between 15 and 22 years old when she was beheaded from…",
        "audio_url": null,
        "description": null,
        "license": "proprietary",
        "attribution": null,
        "truncated": true,
        "guid_hash": "1f1c85de53b5f5463e5e771450537a9675f23639",
        "summary": "Inquest-style inquiry concludes iron age remains are of 15- to 22-year-old female who may have been ritually sacrificed A coroner’s investigation into Northern Ireland ’s most venerable cold case has concluded that the victim was decapitated more than 2,000 years ago. The inquest-style inquiry determined that Ballymacombs More Woman – the name given to iron age remains found in a County Derry bog three years ago – was between 15 and 22 years old when she was beheaded from behind with a bladed weapon.",
